      "claim": "The economic relationship between medieval English lords and peasants was defined by the feudal manorial system, in which peasants owed labor services, rents, and various dues rather than engaging in voluntary market transactions.",
      "evidence": "Manorial court rolls and scholarly syntheses (e.g., R. Hilton, *English and European Manorialism*, 1975) describe the obligations of villeins/serfs to their lord and the lack of free‑market exchange.",
