      "answer": "Yes",
      "reason_rejected": "The modern notion of ‘fair trade’ requires voluntary, equitable exchange between autonomous parties. Feudal serfdom, legal monopolies, and statutes like the Statute of Labourers prevented peasants from freely choosing trading partners or negotiating terms, making systematic fair trade impossible."
